nThe move at **J11** is the winning move because it creates a double threat that leads to an unavoidable win.\n1.  It connects the horizontal stones I11 and K11 to form a **Live 3** (I11-J11-K11), forcing a response to prevent a Live 4.\n2.  It simultaneously aligns with the diagonal stones G8 and I10 to create a lethal setup where playing at H9 next would form a **Live 4** (G8-H9-I10-J11).\nSince the opponent can only block one of these threats, Black will be able to form a winning 4-in-a-row on the subsequent turn.\n\nEvaluation: The move J11 creates two simultaneous threats: extending a horizontal Open 3 and setting up a diagonal Open 4 (at H9). White cannot block both, guaranteeing a win for Black.\n\nAnswer: { "col": "J", "row": 11 }'}
